{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension","id":1336930,"title":"Understanding \"Sphere Logic\" in Mage: the Ascension","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-19T13:17:41-07:00","id":1336930,"title":"Understanding \"Sphere Logic\" in Mage: the Ascension","content":"I have gone through Mage a few times, and several aspects of the Sphere system are still hard to grok.<br /> <br /> I get some of the basic functions of how casting and effects work, and have a sort of cheatsheet down:<br /> <br /> * One Sphere = control over that domain, starting with perception and moving to &quot;godlike feats.&quot;<br /> * You can maintain multiple ongoing spells, but a spell can only have one Effect on it.<br /> * An Effect exists in a &quot;fixed&quot; point of spacetime, unless you use another Sphere to lock the Effect onto a certain Pattern.<br /> * You can only cast the effect in your localized spacetime without the use of Correspondence or Time Spheres.<br /> * You need Prime in order to &quot;create&quot; patterns ex nihilo; you can only &quot;alter/control/link&quot; patterns otherwise.<br /> <br /> This said and done, there are several things I am unsure about how to actually work, and I would rather not have to look up &quot;How Do You Do That,&quot; as I hear there is a lot of skub involved with it. The big one is this:<br /> <br /> Can you create a spell with a &quot;parameterized&quot;/&quot;wildcard&quot; effect? For example, suppose you want to create a spell so that, the next time a person steps through a door, you mentally project&quot;Hello, {that person's name}&quot; to {that person's} mind.<br /> <br /> From strict RAW, this looks like it would need two seperate: One to determine the target's name, and one to broadcast a message to the person who just stepped in. The problem is, I don't see any way for the &quot;output&quot; of the first effect (determining the target's name) to be supplied as an &quot;input&quot; to the message broadcast to the target's mind.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T13:49:35-07:00","id":1336935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicJuggler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension#post1336930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* You can maintain multiple ongoing spells, but a spell can only have one Effect on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just something that seems worth amending: You can maintain a limited number of ongoing spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you create a spell with a &quot;parameterized&quot;/&quot;wildcard&quot; effect? For example, suppose you want to create a spell so that, the next time a person steps through a door, you mentally project&quot;Hello, {that person's name}&quot; to {that person's} mind. </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> This specific example takes Correspondence and Mind (and maybe more depending on how paranoid your mage is). Correspondence is used to create the spatial parameter of the spell (when X walks through or into a specific point in space), as well as linking the spell to the space itself (rather than, say, using Matter to link it to the doorway, which you could do.... but why bother). Mind both detects the specific mind of the person once they meet the parameter if this is pre-programmed for an individual or scans their mind for a name (this is were paranoid mages would add more to such a spell to help make sure they're targeting the right individual and not a faker), and projects the mental thought into the target's mind.<br /> <br /> It is, in essence, a very nice variation on using a Ward/Ban effect as a greeting instead of a warning or actual barrier.<br /> <br /> I think what's hanging you up is, &quot;...but a spell can only have one Effect on it&quot;<br /> <br /> This is true, but not as hard as you're making it to be. You're viewing this as two Effects because it's two basic/common Effects. Effects are allowed to be far more complicated than most of the sample ones. They key is (and this is not a simple hard line to draw sometimes) are you adding conditions to one Effect to create a more complex Effect, or stacking multiple spells together.<br /> <br /> Some of this is going to also come down to the mage and how they perceive things/want things to be done.<br /> <br /> The way to keep this a single Effect is to, at least mechanically, treat the core effect as, &quot;project the target's name as they perceive it into their minds as part of a message,&quot; this is a single coherent effect. The addition parameters such as giving it the power to read their minds, and locking the spell to a specific point in space are adding complexity to this concept, rather than adding new things.<br /> <br /> The one Effect rule is meant to stop things like trying to case a healing spell on your friend, and a fire ball at your enemy in one spell. It's not one cohesive if complex Effect concept, it's two different ones that would be convenient to do at the same time.<br /> <br /> In practice, don't sweat this one too much. Doing it as multiple spells has some pluses and minuses, as does doing it as a single spell. Esp. for something a mage has plenty of time to set up, a single spell is generally better for them, but most of the time it's not going to be the difference between the characters doing what they're trying to do or not, just how much work it takes to get there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T13:55:09-07:00","id":1336936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicJuggler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension#post1336930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you create a spell with a &quot;parameterized&quot;/&quot;wildcard&quot; effect? For example, suppose you want to create a spell so that, the next time a person steps through a door, you mentally project&quot;Hello, {that person's name}&quot; to {that person's} mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That is what the Time 4 triggers are for. In this case you would use Time 4 to make the trigger/hanging effect, you'd use Matter 2 to tie the effect to the doorway, Life 1 to associate it with any lifeform moving through the doorway (life 3 might be specific enough to make it work on people only), and Mind 3 for the mental message. You can get by with Forces instead of Mind if you want to make it an audible message. No need for Prime to create the sound ex nihilo, since you can use another force nearby to convert and use depending on level.<br /> <br /> The only really tricky part would be the Name...in that case, it might be wiser to stick with Mind instead of Forces. Mental message that also tries to discern the name from the subject.<br /> <br /> All this, by the way, pretty much counts as a single effect. The effect is 'Personally greet people as they step through the doorway'.<br /> <br /> Don't be too restrictive in what counts as a single effect..it's very blurry borders when it comes to those, and very much ST decision. If it serves a single purpose, it usually can be called a single effect.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> To say, Heavy Arms' solution is more elegant, as it replaces a lot of the Sphere necessities with Correspondence. I still say it requires TIme 4, though.<br /> But, It just shows you a thing many people experienced with Mage will tell you: There are always multiple ways to skin a cat.<br /> Heck, we had a thread where we tried to figure out all possible ways to literally skin a cat with magick. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-19-2019, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T14:13:04-07:00","id":1336939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have gone through Mage a few times, and several aspects of the Sphere system are still hard to grok. </div> </div> </div>Welcome to Mage. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This said and done, there are several things I am unsure about how to actually work, and I would rather not have to look up &quot;How Do You Do That,&quot; as I hear there is a lot of skub involved with it. </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's not *that* bad. I think there's a general consensus about what people dislikes from it (sphere taxes and the rules about vampires, mainly) and the rest it's kosher. For veterans it come as mostly obvious stuff (a lot of it was on previous suplements) with some cool ideas and a big amount of needless complications.<br /> <br /> That being said, it may help to understand a few things with it's examples and ideas.<br /> <br /> As for your dilema, I would point to Heavy Arms excelent answer<br /> <br /> Just to clarify, the &quot;input&quot; comes from the &quot;sensory magick&quot;. You can use any spell that would serve to gather information to &quot;inform&quot; your magick. Just as you can cast the spell from information that exists in your own mind (say, to project your own toughts), you can also cast from information gathered elsewhere as long as your magick can access it (say, in this case, to project what's on the mind of another).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-19-2019, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T14:14:57-07:00","id":1336940,"title":"","content":"If I am understandspeaking, it's not so much that an effect is a single &quot;Atomic&quot; action (&quot;Read target's mind&quot;) so much as it is a function with a single functional output, correct? <br /> <br /> E.x. a Virtual Adept with the Correspondence Sphere could instead use Forces to encode the person's name in trinary file format to save with a timestamp in an external datastore, while a separate filewatcher thread could read the incoming name, deparse to string, prepend with &quot;Hello,&quot; then broadcast an electrical signal which a second spell effect (time, correspondence, forces, mind) would then transform into a mental impulse to send to &quot;the person&quot; in a secondary stacked ward-location? This would count as two separate spells, correct? (One to &quot;output&quot; the spell into filedata, one to convert a string into a mental message)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T14:51:34-07:00","id":1336946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicJuggler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension?p=1336940#post1336940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I am understandspeaking, it's not so much that an effect is a single &quot;Atomic&quot; action (&quot;Read target's mind&quot;) so much as it is a function with a single functional output, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though to be clear the single functional output can be an &quot;if...else..&quot; function with different outputs as long as it's just one final output.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> E.x. a Virtual Adept with the Correspondence Sphere could instead use Forces to encode the person's name in trinary file format to save with a timestamp in an external datastore, while a separate filewatcher thread could read the incoming name, deparse to string, prepend with &quot;Hello,&quot; then broadcast an electrical signal which a second spell effect (time, correspondence, forces, mind) would then transform into a mental impulse to send to &quot;the person&quot; in a secondary stacked ward-location? This would count as two separate spells, correct? (One to &quot;output&quot; the spell into filedata, one to convert a string into a mental message)? </div> </div> </div><br /> Minor quibble about using Forces alone to encode information like that, but that part is otherwise fine (there's a reason the optional Data Sphere exists).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it's the best way to go about it, but yes, that would be two spells as described. The main reason to do it this way would be that you can edit the name file without having to redo the broadcast program each time. Otherwise you'd have to redo the broadcast program each time you add a name (aka cancel the effect and recast it with new parameters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-19-2019, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:45:23-07:00","id":1337127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicJuggler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension#post1336930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* An Effect exists in a &quot;fixed&quot; point of spacetime, unless you use another Sphere to lock the Effect onto a certain Pattern.<br /> * You can only cast the effect in your localized spacetime without the use of Correspondence or Time Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit of a minor quibble here but it is important. You're using the word 'spacetime' twice here which kind of implies that you're assuming a scientific/real world physics approach to the spell effects. When you take a 'real world' approach to magic you're ignoring the various other paradigms that mage allows for. It's actually quite hard to 'think like a mage' when working out spells and their rules but it is an essential exercise to understand that the same effect can be attained through different paradigms (and that some paradigms are innately 'easier' to work with certain effects).<br /> <br /> Take the classic fire(ball/bolt/etc) spell - to a technocrat it's a high tech flamethrower/plasma projector, to a traditionalist it's tapping into hermetic forces, to an alchemist it's combining potent ingredients, and to an infernalist it's channelling demonic power.<br /> <br /> Each of those paradigms has a different sort of 'physics' and flipping viewpoints between them is an important skill to master for Mage players and storytellers. It's all to easy to fall back into thinking about effects with the modern scientific approach we have been taught at school, but mage is multi-angled and works really well when we put aside our modern thinking and open up to the paradigms in the game.<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot to say, because I'm not calling you out for having wrongfun, that if you're happy with the modern approach then go for it, I like the way Mage allows you to use different mindsets to solve a problem but it's not the 'one true way'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 09-21-2019, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T20:45:16-07:00","id":1337441,"title":"","content":"FWIW, I also think one should consider the significance of the effect when setting sphere requirements, rather than trying to parse the exact physical mechanics. It's magic, afterall. You can always add more specificity and talk yourself into more extreme requirements, but I don't find that to be in the spirit of things.<br /> <br /> To me, the key elements of the proposed spell are that it's a telepathic message, and that it waits. As such, I'd say Mind 2 (maybe 3 to add in the &quot;name&quot; blank to the message, but I'd say that's within scope for the Mind sphere alone if you just make it &quot;whatever the mind calls itself&quot;), plus Time 2 or 3 to delay it until the condition is met. Mind 1 can detect the presence of a mind so that's good enough for the trigger. I wouldn't call for Correspondence or Matter unless you wanted to, say, embed the message specifically in the doorframe itself (so that it will still work if, say, someone moved it to another building), and I wouldn't call for Life unless there was some biological property (however specific) in the trigger that Mind alone couldn't handle. E.g., a woman, a pregnant woman, a pregnant woman with a cold, etc. Ironically, being maximally broad (&quot;any conscious mind&quot;) or very specific (&quot;my friend Dave&quot;) would fit comfortably in Mind, you'd only need other spheres to come down in the middle, or to get even MORE specific (Dave, but only if he's bleeding from a cut on his left hand)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 09-22-2019, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T03:28:41-07:00","id":1337461,"title":"","content":"The main reason to go with Correspondence is that, like a minor ward, it can be done at Correspondence 2. Time triggers are flat out a Time 4 thing.<br /> <br /> The significance of the effect goes into how many successes it takes to cast more than what Sphere ranks are required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T09:12:19-07:00","id":1337644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension?p=1337461#post1337461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason to go with Correspondence is that, like a minor ward, it can be done at Correspondence 2. Time triggers are flat out a Time 4 thing.<br /> <br /> The significance of the effect goes into how many successes it takes to cast more than what Sphere ranks are required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I still see it as more of an effect of time than place; if you were standing in the room when they walked in, you wouldn't need Correspondence for the effect. Further, I don't really see it as a proper &quot;time trigger&quot; or even &quot;location trigger&quot;, the trigger comes from Mind. Since I could use Correspondence 2/3 to send you the message *now* but from *far away*, I'd let someome use Time 2/3 to send the message *later* but *right here*.<br /> <br /> But, I will cede that it's reasonable to treat it as a ward too. Different paradigms, different ways of doing similar things, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T10:25:45-07:00","id":1337657,"title":"","content":"The thing is, Time and Correspondence work very differently in the way they treat their influence.<br /> <br /> Time 2 doesn't send anything anywhere. It allows to see stuff, but not to talk or otherwise influence the future/past you're seeing. Time 2 would be WAY more powerful than described if it allowed to interact with other times the same way Corr 2 interacts with other places<br /> <br /> To send the message *later* but *right here* you would need Time 5. If you're literally sending it to the future, that's time travel.<br /> <br /> Time 4 it's used to keep a message (or, in this case, an Effect) *frozen* to be released at a latter time. Time triggers it's an odd way to refer to the act of freezing an effect with Time 4 so it doesn't take place the turn it's casted (like it's normal for most effects). The nature of the *actual* trigger seems to matter little to this (I think it's mentioned somewhere to <b>add </b>Entropy if you want the effect to be triggered by an event, but Time 4 it's pretty constant in Effects that are to take place at a later time).<br /> <br /> So, I have to agree with <i>Heavy Arms</i> and <i>Ambrosia </i>here. Time 4 would be needed to place the message in suspension until something happens, unless you have other way to make the effect *hang* there. And that's the cheapest way using Time alone to define the &quot;delivery&quot;.<br /> <br /> That being said, a houserule to make Time more in line with Correspondence (to allow these sort of &quot;late deliveries&quot; that we call time triggers) wouldn't be a bad idea. I don't think it's op, if we add also the Correspondence precaution of allowing to hang only effects of the same Sphere level as the level of Time used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-24-2019, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T13:37:10-07:00","id":1337688,"title":"","content":"My understanding of different Effect trigger categories:<br /> <br /> Space triggers: Correspondence 3 (piggybacks off warding)<br /> Time triggers: Time 4<br /> General triggers (can include time or space conditions): Time 4 Entropy 2 OR Prime 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T13:58:57-07:00","id":1337695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension?p=1337644#post1337644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I still see it as more of an effect of time than place;</div> </div> </div> </div>For the specific effect being asked about, the conditional parameter is, &quot;as the person walks through the door.&quot; If anything that implies its more an effect of place (the triggering event is a change in spatial positioning, not the precise time at which it occurs).<br /> <br /> It's just that the nature of the system allows multiple ways to do it, and you can do it with Time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you were standing in the room when they walked in, you wouldn't need Correspondence for the effect. </div> </div> </div>You... wouldn't need Time either... without the desire to have it be conditional in the way phrased. If you're just sitting there and want to toss messages into people's heads, you just need Mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Further, I don't really see it as a proper &quot;time trigger&quot; or even &quot;location trigger&quot;, the trigger comes from Mind. </div> </div> </div>But it's not a purely Mind effect because it triggers from not just Mind as stated. If it was just Mind, it would happen as soon as you cast it, where the target it (and they'd have to be within your normal sensory range).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since I could use Correspondence 2/3 to send you the message *now* but from *far away*, I'd let someome use Time 2/3 to send the message *later* but *right here*. </div> </div> </div>If you want to discuss house ruling Time to be less... meh... as a Sphere? I'm all for that, but lets take that to a different thread. It doesn't help people understand how things work RAW to get into house rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension?p=1337657#post1337657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time triggers it's an odd way to refer to the act of freezing an effect with Time 4 so it doesn't take place the turn it's casted (like it's normal for most effects).</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Time trigger,&quot; phrasing mostly comes from what causes the hung spell to activate rather than the act of hanging it to wait. It's less odd when you're thinking of &quot;how am I encoded into the spell when it unfreezes,&quot; instead of the process of freezing it; since freezing it is just having Time 4 and using a very straightforward effect it allows.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension?p=1337688#post1337688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space triggers: Correspondence 3 (piggybacks off warding)</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 at least added a Correspondence 2 level of warding, which is fairly appropriate to this specific effect. In Revised and earlier it would have been Correspondence 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T15:14:50-07:00","id":1337719,"title":"","content":"M20 also requires that whole 'your correspondence must be the same level as the other spheres involved' caveat. So if you want to send a life 5 effect through distance you need correspondence 5. Not sure if that would apply to a warding effect. (Maybe not?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T01:37:18-07:00","id":1337776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension?p=1337719#post1337719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 also requires that whole 'your correspondence must be the same level as the other spheres involved' caveat</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a new caveat by any means - Revised introduced that, pretty much. (Can't find it in SC, 2nd or 1st ed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T09:54:33-07:00","id":1337821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension?p=1337695#post1337695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 at least added a Correspondence 2 level of warding, which is fairly appropriate to this specific effect. In Revised and earlier it would have been Correspondence 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've always had warding against Correspondence effects at level 2--I was using the colloquial use of &quot;warding&quot; which Mage calls Banning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T09:31:29-07:00","id":1339391,"title":"","content":"In other words, what I am seeing from this is:<br /> <br /> Correspondence as a warding function is dependent on the actual effect being hooked into warding in M20. So some godlike feat (E.x. Forces 5: &quot;transmute gravity into gamma radiation in this localized space&quot;) would require Correspondence 5 to contain it. The &quot;metaphysical&quot; logic would be that the Ward/ban is acting as a &quot;Container&quot; for such a trigger.<br /> <br /> With this in mind, I think it would be safe to make a few tweaks to Time and Entropy in turn.<br /> <br /> 1) If the Effect involves any &quot;Unknown&quot; Patterns at the time of casting, then Entropy is needed equal to the highest effect you want to use. For example, &quot;Sense the thoughts of the closest person in the next room&quot; (Mind 1) would also need Entropy 1 (and Correspondence), because you don't necessarily know who is &quot;the closest person&quot; in the next room, or if there is even a person in said room. Plus if there are two equidistant people...<br /> 2) Time is not a &quot;container&quot; in the same way that Correspondence is. I would instead be ok with tweaking the rules for &quot;Time&quot; so that you can alter it so rather than needing Time 4 to hang triggers, you can do several levels of increasing precision:<br /> -Time 2 lets you do simple &quot;time-delays&quot; for Effects to begin and/or end.<br /> -Time 3 lets an effect recursively call itself, once per turn, until a time 2 end clause is reached; the maximum duration of the overall effect does not change, but this can be used alongside Entropy/Correspondence for the creation of fractaling spells.<br /> -Time 4 lets you add &quot;Pause on Condition for X duration&quot; qualifiers to effects.<br /> -Time 5 lets you &quot;Synchronize&quot; multiple effects, handle countdowns and listeners, etc.<br /> 3) Thus, a Zone of &quot;Hello Person-name&quot; would require Mind 2 (Read/project), Correspondence 2 (the zone of Hello), and Entropy 2 (because the &quot;pattern&quot; of the person being broadcast to is unknown at the time). If the effect was to simply etch the person's name into a predetermined block of stone, it would be Mind 1, Matter 2, Entropy 1 instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","user":"MagicJuggler","date":". 10-04-2019, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T10:28:02-07:00","id":1339401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicJuggler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336930-understanding-sphere-logic-in-mage-the-ascension?p=1339391#post1339391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) If the Effect involves any &quot;Unknown&quot; Patterns at the time of casting, then Entropy is needed equal to the highest effect you want to use. For example, &quot;Sense the thoughts of the closest person in the next room&quot; (Mind 1) would also need Entropy 1 (and Correspondence), because you don't necessarily know who is &quot;the closest person&quot; in the next room, or if there is even a person in said room. Plus if there are two equidistant people...</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy wouldn't be necessary because Correspondence 1 can sense everything that's in an area and can opperate with concepts like &quot;close/far&quot;, while Mind 1 can sense that the &quot;objects&quot; detected with Corr in the area are &quot;minds&quot;. You could imagine Corr 1/Mind 1 as a &quot;radar of consciences that are nearby&quot;, having that info it's easy to determine trough distance (Corr) alone who has the closest mind<br /> And if nobody it's there, the spell simply shows nothing in the &quot;radar&quot;, you could infer that there's no thoughts on the room...or they're hidden somehow. Now, if you were trying to &quot;do&quot; something to that mind (or it's owner), the spell simply 'does nothing'. To a C# programmer: it returns NullReferenceException :P .<br /> <br /> Entropy could be added to, say, detect the mind of the one that's most likely to win the lotery or to detect the mind of the one that's going to leave the next room first, or (in a &quot;mystery murder&quot; sort of scenario) the one that's going to die first (That's very Entropy. Time 2 could do this too, but then you would need Correspondence 2, so it's harder)<br /> <br /> It's not so much to opperate on unknown Patterns, but on unknown &quot;factors&quot; (preferably if these depend of chance or are related to death or decay)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Time 3 lets an effect recursively call itself, once per turn, until a time 2 end clause is reached; the maximum duration of the overall effect does not change, but this can be used alongside Entropy/Correspondence for the creation of fractaling spells. </div> </div> </div>I think this IS possible, but it could (likely would) be incredibly, amazingly, paradoxical. It's not just Vulgar, Time 3 recursivity has it's own Paradox rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Thus, a Zone of &quot;Hello Person-name&quot; would require Mind 2 (Read/project), Correspondence 2 (the zone of Hello), and Entropy 2 (because the &quot;pattern&quot; of the person being broadcast to is unknown at the time) </div> </div> </div>I don't think Entropy would be necessary because you don't care about the circumstances of the person that gets the memo. The Mind magick combined with the minnor ward &quot;sweeps&quot; the whole barrier that it's the door all the time and catches whoever pass trough it. If you wanted the message to chage depending on some other factor (say, give a different message to your enemies) then Entropy could be called for","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-04-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}